><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20250709104431+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="7247d5bd-4214-4841-acdb-5bf31a389a26" date="D:20250709104431+10'00'" name="9d344897-fe80-44ed-ab6a-5ce6f0f4316a" icon="Comment" page="8" rect="305.329834,284.282715,329.329834,308.282715" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Practitioners are&#xD;recommended to reduce the number of individual training&#xD;preparedness variables collected into three distinct&#xD;categories of psychological, physiological, and physical.&#xD;This study provides knowledge that can be used to educate&#xD;coaches, practitioners, and sporting organizations to adjust&#xD;training, monitoring, recovery, and athlete health interventions&#xD;following the provision of tailored data in elite and&#xD;pre-elite females athletes.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="8" rect="595.276001,216.282715,779.276001,308.282715"
/></text
